From eac66f177afe7348de23ac084ffe0d58c15aee63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Silva <samuel@ossystems.com.br>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:20:34 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] feat(server): the host can manage the agents' memory

T3 Code caps the agents slice at a share of the RAM the machine has when an
agent starts. A VM whose host plugs memory as it runs short starts small: in
one that boots with 2 GiB and may grow to 16, agents were capped at 1.5 GiB,
or throttled at 1 GiB with swap, and the cap only caught up at the next agent
launch. An administrator's own drop-in for the slice loses to the runtime
override too.

T3CODE_AGENT_SLICE_MEMORY_POLICY=host-managed leaves the slice's memory alone.
Unset or automatic keeps the caps; anything else warns and keeps them. Scopes,
OOM reporting and the parent slice's CPU, IO and task limits are unchanged.
The same option is proposed upstream in pingdotgg/t3code#24717.
